---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj39.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — the Consolidated Cash Flow Statement Base Standard" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Why \"Part 3\" — a History of Staged Amendment" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Likely Drivers — Coordination With the Leases and Interim Reporting Reforms" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Direct vs Indirect Method — the Underlying Framework" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Lease Payment Classification in the Cash Flow Statement" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="active"
    title="Recency Note (October 2025)"
    explanation="RECENCY NOTE: Issued October 16, 2025 alongside ASBJ Statement No. 37, 38, and 40 — details should be cross-checked against ASBJ's current published materials."
    link=""
    linkText=""
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A refinement to the group cash flow statement preparation standard</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 39 is the THIRD stage ("Part 3") of PARTIAL amendments to Japan's UNDERLYING standard governing the PREPARATION of consolidated Statements of Cash Flows — the J-GAAP counterpart to IAS 7 / ASC 230 internationally. LIKE the earlier staged reforms seen elsewhere in this poster series (e.g. Retirement Benefits, Statements No. 3/14/19), Japan's cash flow statement guidance has EVOLVED through SUCCESSIVE, INCREMENTAL amendment stages RATHER than a single comprehensive rewrite.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope — the Consolidated Cash Flow Statement Base Standard</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Groups preparing a consolidated Statement of Cash Flows</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to PARENT companies preparing a CONSOLIDATED Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書) — the primary statement PRESENTING a group's cash INFLOWS and OUTFLOWS, classified into OPERATING, INVESTING, and FINANCING activities.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Why "Part 3" — a History of Staged Amendment</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A recurring ASBJ pattern of incremental, multi-stage refinement</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The "Part 3" designation INDICATES this is the THIRD in a SEQUENCE of partial amendments to the underlying consolidated cash flow statement standard — CONSISTENT with the SAME broader ASBJ pattern of PREFERRING incremental, staged refinement over comprehensive single-instance rewrites, ALSO seen in the retirement benefits reform (Statements No. 3, 14, 19) and the tax effect accounting amendments (No. 28, and now No. 40, "Part 2" — see the companion poster).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>Likely Drivers — Coordination With the Leases and Interim Reporting Reforms</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">A cash flow statement update reflecting the new leases and interim reforms</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Given this Statement's ISSUANCE alongside the BROADER October 2025 interim reporting package (No. 37, 38, and 40), and given the SIGNIFICANT new lease liabilities/right-of-use assets introduced by ASBJ Statement No. 34 (see the companion poster), this "Part 3" amendment PLAUSIBLY addresses HOW cash flows relating to the NEW on-balance-sheet lease model (e.g. splitting lease payments between the PRINCIPAL portion, classified as a FINANCING activity, and the INTEREST portion) should be CLASSIFIED within the consolidated Statement of Cash Flows — CONSISTENT with how IFRS 16's introduction ALSO required corresponding cash flow statement CLASSIFICATION guidance internationally. This inference reflects the SURROUNDING context of the COORDINATED reform package; the PRECISE scope should be confirmed against ASBJ's own published text.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Direct vs Indirect Method — the Underlying Framework</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Both methods remain available for operating activities</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The UNDERLYING J-GAAP consolidated cash flow statement standard permits EITHER the DIRECT method (presenting MAJOR classes of gross cash receipts/payments) or the INDIRECT method (starting from NET profit, adjusting for non-cash items and working capital changes) for OPERATING activities — broadly CONSISTENT with the SAME choice available under IAS 7 internationally, with the INDIRECT method being the MORE commonly used approach in PRACTICE.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Lease Payment Classification in the Cash Flow Statement</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Splitting lease payments between principal and interest</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A lease payment under the new on-balance-sheet model</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A group makes an annual lease payment of ¥20,000,000 under a lease recognised as a right-of-use asset and lease liability per ASBJ Statement No. 34, comprising ¥17,000,000 of principal repayment and ¥3,000,000 of interest.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">Consistent with the LIKELY direction of this Statement's amendments, the ¥17,000,000 PRINCIPAL portion is classified as a FINANCING activity outflow, while the ¥3,000,000 INTEREST portion follows the group's GENERAL policy for interest classification (typically operating or financing) — REFLECTING how the new on-balance-sheet lease model REQUIRES corresponding cash flow statement classification guidance.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 39 addresses</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Classification of cash flows relating to leases recognised under the new on-balance-sheet model</span>
          <span>Reconciliation between cash and cash equivalents and the Balance Sheet</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Classification of interest cash flows as operating or financing activities</span>
              <span>Splitting lease payments between principal and interest components for cash flow presentation</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Generally minimal — this is primarily a classification and presentation matter</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 7</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The GENERAL structure of J-GAAP's consolidated cash flow statement (operating/investing/financing classification, direct/indirect method choice) is BROADLY converged with IAS 7. The SPECIFIC lease-payment classification question THIS Statement likely addresses PARALLELS the SAME classification guidance IFRS 16's introduction REQUIRED internationally, GIVEN the shared underlying shift toward on-balance-sheet lease accounting.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every relevant cash flow event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Lease payment cash flows</span>
            <span><span class="badge bc">SCF</span></span>
            <span>Principal portion as financing, interest per general policy</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 34</span>
            <span>Leases — supplies the new on-balance-sheet lease liability this Statement's amendments likely address for cash flow classification</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 37</span>
            <span>The general interim reporting framework issued as part of the same coordinated reform package</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The primary statement presenting a group's cash inflows and outflows, classified into operating, investing, and financing activities.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
